※ pl4g-test: compile=fail
※ pl4g-test: expect-diag 4416 LANG_MATCH_BINDS_NOTHING

※ An arm binds a name to the value its alternative carries.  The error of a
※ result whose error carries nothing has none, so the name would stand for
※ nothing; the pattern without the parentheses is how it is taken.

let hundred: mut u8 = 100u8
let seven: mut u8 = 7u8

@[startup]
fn main() → u8:
    match hundred ÷ seven:
        u8(q):
            return q
        ⊥(e):
            return 1u8
